<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lae</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lae is the second-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a> and capital of Morobe Province, at the mouth of the Markham River on the Huon Gulf. It grew in the 1920s and 1930s as the air base for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulolo">Bulolo</a> goldfields, and Amelia Earhart took off from there on her last flight in 1937. Destroyed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, it was rebuilt as the country's main industrial centre and port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lae.jpg" alt="Lae" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lae_City_and_Markham_River_(aerial_view).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
